          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Weight Is the Hidden Cost</h3>

          <p>
            Weight is the hidden cost of capacity. A 25,000mAh bank weighs as much as two or three phones and sits like a brick in a small bag. Many experienced travelers carry a 10,000mAh bank daily and leave a larger one in the hotel room or the checked-in carry-on to refill it. Two smaller banks also give you a backup if one fails or gets confiscated, which a single big bank does not.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Stay Under 100Wh for Flying</h3>

          <p>
            Do not buy past the 100Wh line for flying. Banks between 100 and 160Wh technically fly with airline approval, but getting approval at check-in is inconsistent, rules vary by carrier, and the extra 20 to 50Wh rarely justifies the hassle. For road trips and camping, though, size is unrestricted, and a small <a href="/best-portable-power-station-for-camping/">camping power station</a> gives you AC outlets and several times the capacity of any bank.
          </p>
