          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most travelers, the Anker Nano with its built-in cable is the right bank: two phone charges, no cable to forget, and nowhere near any airline limit. iPhone users who want to charge while walking should take the Anker MagGo instead, and anyone carrying a laptop should step up to the Anker 25K with built-in cables or the UGREEN Nexode for less money.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, keep it under 100Wh, keep it in your carry-on, and check your airline's in-flight rules before you board. Buy from a brand that prints honest watt-hour ratings, pack a universal USB-C wall charger, and you will not think about your phone battery again for the rest of the trip.
